windows-dllmain-export: a fix to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

DllMain is the Windows loader's entry point, not an API for another DLL to import. Exporting it puts it in
sycl9.lib and sycl.lib; lld-link warns that it skips the imported DllMain on every link. Keep the entry point
and its address for isLinkedStatically, but do not export it. Windows execution is unverified.
---
diff --git a/sycl/source/detail/global_handler.cpp b/sycl/source/detail/global_handler.cpp
--- a/sycl/source/detail/global_handler.cpp
+++ b/sycl/source/detail/global_handler.cpp
@@ -379,9 +379,8 @@ void GlobalHandler::shutdown() {
 }
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
-extern "C" __SYCL_EXPORT BOOL WINAPI DllMain(HINSTANCE hinstDLL,
-                                             DWORD fdwReason,
-                                             LPVOID lpReserved) {
+extern "C" BOOL WINAPI DllMain(HINSTANCE hinstDLL, DWORD fdwReason,
+                               LPVOID lpReserved) {
